</td></tr><tr></tr><tr><td><code>\<space></space></code></td><td>space</td><td><code>\negmedspace</code></td><td>- ⁴∕₁₈ em space</td></tr><tr></tr><tr><td><code>\nobreakspace</code></td><td>non-breaking space</td><td><code>\negthickspace</code></td><td>- ⁵∕₁₈ em space</td></tr><tr></tr><tr><td><code>\space</code></td><td>space</td><td><code>\mathstrut</code></td><td><code>\vphantom&lbrace;(&rbrace;</code></td></tr><tr></tr></tbody></table> <p>Notes:<br><code>distance</code> will accept any of the KaTeX units.<br><code>\kern</code>, <code>\mkern</code>, <code>\mskip</code>, and <code>\hspace</code> accept unbraced distances, as in: <code>\kern1em</code>.<br><code>\mkern</code> and <code>\mskip</code> will not work in text mode and both will        write a console warning for any unit except <code>mu</code>.</p></details> <details><summary>Logic and Set Theory</summary> <table><tbody><tr><!----><td><!----><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span></span></span></span></span><!----> <code>\forall</code></td><!----><td><!----><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∁</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\complement</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.825em;"></span><span class="mord amsrm">∁</span></span></span></span></span><!----> <code>\complement</code></td><!----><td><!----><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="kat